1
00:00:00,100 --> 00:00:02,350
Tour of the Console.

2
00:00:02,300 --> 00:00:05,450
Know where everything is before you touch anything.

3
00:00:05,450 --> 00:00:08,125
Eight Zones of the X32.

4
00:00:08,125 --> 00:00:14,575
Channel strip section: Gain, low cut, EQ, and monitor sends for the selected channel — top left.

5
00:00:14,575 --> 00:00:20,725
Screen & knobs: The color screen shows what section is selected; knobs below it change the values.

6
00:00:20,725 --> 00:00:25,812
Scenes & USB: Load the Sunday scene here and plug in a flash drive to record.

7
00:00:25,812 --> 00:00:30,150
Layer buttons: Choose which 16 channels the faders control.

8
00:00:30,150 --> 00:00:33,512
For Sunday, keep CH 1-16 lit.

9
00:00:33,512 --> 00:00:39,112
Channel strips: Each strip has SELECT, SOLO, MUTE buttons and a motorized fader.

10
00:00:39,112 --> 00:00:44,000
Sends on Fader button: Turns faders into monitor mix controls when lit.

11
00:00:44,000 --> 00:00:46,325
Always exit when done.

12
00:00:46,325 --> 00:00:49,887
Bus / DCA faders: Far-right faders.

13
00:00:49,887 --> 00:00:53,100
Control monitor mixes and channel groups.

14
00:00:53,100 --> 00:00:58,612
Main LR fader: Tallest fader on the right — sets overall volume to the main speakers.

15
00:00:58,612 --> 00:01:02,675
Four things every volunteer must know: SELECT picks the channel.

16
00:01:02,675 --> 00:01:06,412
MUTE (lit red) = channel is OFF.

17
00:01:06,412 --> 00:01:08,962
SOLO listens in headphones.

18
00:01:08,962 --> 00:01:11,500
FADER sets the room volume.

19
00:01:11,500 --> 00:01:14,512
Know these four and you can run a service.

20
00:01:14,512 --> 00:01:16,337
Wrong faders?

21
00:01:16,337 --> 00:01:18,525
Check the LAYER buttons.

22
00:01:18,525 --> 00:01:21,500
The faders follow whatever layer is lit.

23
00:01:21,500 --> 00:01:26,425
For Sunday service, CH 1-16 must always be your active layer.

